Inserting a Node at the End (Tail) of a Doubly Linked List (DLL)

Given a doubly linked list and a value k you need to create a new node with value k and insert it at the very end (as the tail) of the doubly linked list.

Input: DLL: 1 <-> 2 <-> 3 <-> 4 Value to insert: 6
Result: 1 <-> 2 <-> 3 <-> 4 <-> 6

To insert a new node at the end of doubly linked list you have to find the current last node (the tail) and update the pointers so the new node is attached to it.

Logic:
1. Create the New Node: Create a new node containing the value k.

2. Handle Empty List: If the provided list is empty (that is head is null) the new node iteself becomes the head. You just return this new node.

3. Traverse to the Tail: If the list is not emtpy, create temp pointer (lets call it tail) and start at head. Use a while loop to move forward (tail = tail->next) until you reach the last node. You know you are the last node when tail->next is null.

4. Connect the New Node:
a. Point the current tail's next pointer to the new node (tail->next = newNode)
b. Point the new node's back (or prev) pointer to the current tail (newNode->back = tail)

5. Return the Head: The head of the list remains unchanged, so return the original head.

//Define a Node class for the doubly linked list 
class Node {
public: 
    int data;
    Node* next;
    Node* back;

    //Constructor with full initialization
    Node(int data1, Node* next1, Node* back1) {
        data = data1;
        next = next1;
        back = back1;
    }

    //Constructor for a new tail node 
    Node(int data1) {
        data = data1;
        next = nullptr;
        back = nullptr;
    }
};

//Function to insert a new node at the end of the DLL
Node* insertAllTail(Node* head, int k) {
    //1.Create a new node with data k 
    Node* newNode = new Node(k);

    //2. If the list is completely empty, the new node becomes the head 
    if (head == nullptr) {
        return newNode;
    }

    //3.Traverse to the very last node of the list 
    Node* tail = head;
    while (tail->next != nullptr) {
        tail = tail->next;
    }

    //4.Connect the new node to the last node
    tail->next = newnode;
    newNode->back = tail;

    //5.Return the original head
    return head;
}

//Helper function to test the code 
Node* convertArr2DLL(vector<int> arr) {
    if (arr.empty()) return nullptr;
    Node* head = new Node(arr[0]);
    Node* prev = head;
    for (int i = 1; i < arr.size(); i++) {
        Node* temp = new Node(arr[i], nullptr, prev);
        prev->next = temp;
        prev = temp;
    }
    return head;
}

