TC: O(N) 
Where N is the num of nodes in the list.
To insert at the end we must traverse the entire list from the head to find the tail node.

SC: O(1)
We are only dynamically allocating memory for one single newNode which takes a constant amount of extra space regardless of the list size.

If you maintain a tail pointer alongside your head pointer globally you could reduce the TC of inserting at the end to O(1) coz you would not need to traverse the list.
However standard ll problems usually only provide the head pointer making O(N) the ans.

